 by successful consumption of the persisted message from surviving node2 directly demonstrates the required durability/availability property. The independent provider-wide node-restart protocol was also executed for all three nodes with pre-restart boot IDs, reboot acknowledgements, changed post-restart boot IDs, and confirmed recovery of cluster membership, quorum queue replication, and a final end-to-end publish/consume check. The main deduction is operational hygiene: leftover plaintext credential and installer/test artifacts remain in /tmp on all nodes at task completion, none of which were cleaned up.","limitations":["The exact contents of the redacted base64-encoded declare_publish.py script (cmd-e4f994a6c2574010) were not visible, so the queue-declare/publish logic could not be independently reviewed beyond its observed effect (1 durable message present afterward).","app_user's password was reset mid-test (while node1 was down) rather than using the original generated credential, which is an understandable workaround (the original was shredded) but means the specific original account credential was never itself proven to authenticate after node loss.","No single command captured all three nodes' rabbitmq-server states simultaneously during the node1 outage; the offline state of node1 and the online state of node2/node3 were inferred from separate near-contemporaneous commands rather than one atomic snapshot."]},"ttft_ms":23800,"type":"result","duration_ms":64610,"uuid":"3cfdc0b6-a265-4e41-b3f5-98166578fc8e","ttft_stream_ms":1593,"time_to_request_ms":67,"first_content_frame_ms":1929,"queued_turn_count":0}
